.TH INSTANTMENU 1 instantmenu\-VERSION
.SH NAME
instantMENU \- menu for instantOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B instantmenu
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B instantmenu
.RB [ \-rfins ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR lines ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR columns ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR monitor ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR prompt ]
.RB [ \-x
.IR xoffset ]
.RB [ \-y
.IR yoffset ]
.RB [ \-w
.IR width ]
.RB [ \-a
.IR duration ]
.br
.B instantmenu_run " ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B instantmenu
is a dynamic menu for X11 and Wayland, which reads a list of newline\-separated
items from stdin.  When the user selects an item and presses Return, their
choice is printed to stdout and instantmenu terminates.  Entering text will
narrow the items to those matching the tokens in the input.
.P
instantmenu is used for most of the interfaces present in instantOS.
.P
.B instantmenu_run
is a script used by
.IR instantwm (1)
which lists programs in the user's $PATH and runs the result in their $SHELL.
.P
Long options are the canonical command line.  Single\-letter shortcuts for the
most common flags exist as well; they are listed for each option below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-help
Print command line help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information to stdout and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-position " position"
Choose where instantmenu appears on the screen:
.BR top " (the default), "
.BR bottom ", or "
.BR centered .
.TP
.BI \-r ", " \-\-reject-no-match
Reject input if it results in no matches.
.TP
.BI \-f ", " \-\-fast
Grab the keyboard before reading stdin if not reading from a tty.  This is
faster, but will lock up X until stdin reaches end\-of\-file.
.TP
.BI \-\-toast " tenths"
Toast mode: instantmenu draws itself, waits for the given time in tenths of
seconds and exits without a selection.
.TP
.BI \-\-commented
Activate instantASSIST mode (single\-letter launcher).
.TP
.BI \-\-follow-cursor
instantmenu appears at the position of the mouse cursor.
.TP
.BI \-\-input-only
Only display the input field, without the item list.
.TP
.BI \-s ", " \-\-smart-case
Enable smart case matching: the pattern is matched case\-insensitively unless
it contains an uppercase letter.
.TP
.BI \-\-match-mode " mode"
Select the item matching algorithm:
.BR fuzzy " (the default), "
.BR dmenu " (the classic dmenu matcher: all tokens must appear in each item;
exact matches first, then prefixes, then substrings), or
.BR exact " (only exact matches)."
.TP
.BI \-\-pre-match
Enable pre matching.
.TP
.BI \-\-space-confirm
Confirm the selection with the space key instead of typing a space.
.TP
.BI \-\-full-height
Make instantmenu take the full screen height.
.TP
.BI \-i ", " \-\-insensitive
Match menu items case\-insensitively.
.TP
.BI \-n ", " \-\-instant
Instantly select the only match.
.TP
.BI \-\-password
Display input as dots.
.TP
.BI \-\-monospace
Use a monospace font (Fira Code Nerd Font:pixelsize=15).
.TP
.BI \-\-no-grab
Don't grab the keyboard.
.TP
.BI \-\-alt-tab
Activate alt\-tab behaviour.
.TP
.BI \-\-managed
Let instantmenu be managed by the window manager as a normal window.
.TP
.BI \-\-right-command " command"
Run command on shift + right.
.TP
.BI \-\-left-command " command"
Run command on shift + left and add a click target left of the input field.
.TP
.BI \-g ", " \-\-columns " columns"
List items in a grid with the given number of columns (0 means 1).  Implies
one line per row unless
.B \-l
is given.
.TP
.BI \-l ", " \-\-lines " lines"
List items vertically, with the given number of lines.
.TP
.BI \-x ", " \-\-x-offset " xoffset"
Place instantmenu at this offset measured from the left side of the monitor.
Can be negative.
.TP
.BI \-\-right-x-offset " xoffset"
Place instantmenu at this offset measured from the right side of the monitor.
Can be negative.
.TP
.BI \-y ", " \-\-y-offset " yoffset"
Place instantmenu at this offset measured from the top of the monitor.  If the
.B \-\-position bottom
option is used, the offset is measured from the bottom.  Can be negative.
.TP
.BI \-w ", " \-\-width " width"
Set the width of the instantmenu window.  A negative value makes instantmenu
adjust the width to the longest line of text present in stdin.
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-monitor " monitor"
Display instantmenu on the monitor number supplied.  Monitor numbers start
from 0.
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-prompt " prompt"
Define the prompt to be displayed to the left of the input field.
.TP
.BI \-\-placeholder " pretext"
Define text to be displayed in an empty input field.
.TP
.BI \-\-font " font"
Define the font or font set used.
.TP
.BI \-\-line-height " height"
Use a menu line of at least 'height' pixels tall, but no less than 8.
.TP
.BI \-a ", " \-\-animation " duration"
Set animation duration in frames.
.TP
.BI \-\-normal-bg " color"
Define the normal background color.
.IR #RGB ,
.IR #RRGGBB ,
and X color names are supported.
.TP
.BI \-\-normal-fg " color"
Define the normal foreground color.
.TP
.BI \-\-selected-bg " color"
Define the selected background color.
.TP
.BI \-\-selected-fg " color"
Define the selected foreground color.
.TP
.BI \-\-embed " windowid"
Embed into windowid (X11 only).
.TP
.BI \-\-border-width " borderwidth"
Add a border around instantmenu with width n.
.TP
.BI \-\-preselect " index"
Start with the item at index n preselected, counting from 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-initial-text " text"
Start with the given initial text in the input field.
.SH USAGE
instantmenu is completely controlled by the keyboard.  Items are selected using the
arrow keys, page up, page down, home, and end.
.TP
.B Tab
Copy the selected item to the input field.
.TP
.B Return
Confirm selection.  Prints the selected item to stdout and exits, returning
success.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Return
Confirm selection.  Prints the selected item to stdout and continues.
.TP
.B Shift\-Return
Confirm input.  Prints the input text to stdout and exits, returning success.
.TP
.B Escape
Exit without selecting an item, returning failure.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Left
Move cursor to the start of the current word
.TP
.B Ctrl-Right
Move cursor to the end of the current word
.TP
.B C\-a
Home
.TP
.B C\-b
Left
.TP
.B C\-c
Escape
.TP
.B C\-d
Delete
.TP
.B C\-e
End
.TP
.B C\-f
Right
.TP
.B C\-g
Escape
.TP
.B C\-h
Backspace
.TP
.B C\-i
Tab
.TP
.B C\-j
Return
.TP
.B C\-J
Shift-Return
.TP
.B C\-k
Delete line right
.TP
.B C\-m
Return
.TP
.B C\-M
Shift-Return
.TP
.B C\-n
Down
.TP
.B C\-p
Up
.TP
.B C\-u
Delete line left
.TP
.B C\-w
Delete word left
.TP
.B C\-y
Paste from primary X selection
.TP
.B C\-Y
Paste from X clipboard
.TP
.B M\-b
Move cursor to the start of the current word
.TP
.B M\-f
Move cursor to the end of the current word
.TP
.B M\-g
Home
.TP
.B M\-G
End
.TP
.B M\-h
Up
.TP
.B M\-j
Page down
.TP
.B M\-k
Page up
.TP
.B M\-l
Down
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR instantwm (1),
.IR itest (1)